          <h1>CLI reference</h1>
          <p>Every command reads <code>config.kdl</code> from the current directory (or the path given to <code>--config</code>) and accepts the global flags below.</p>
          <h3>Commands</h3>
          <dl>
            <dt><code>baudelaire build</code></dt>
            <dd>Compile the site into <code>dist</code>. Incremental by default. This is the default command, so bare <code>baudelaire</code> builds too.</dd>
            <dt><code>baudelaire serve</code></dt>
            <dd>Build, serve <code>dist</code> over HTTP, watch for changes, and live-reload the browser. Flags: <code>--port</code>, <code>--bind</code>, <code>--open</code>, <code>--no-watch</code>.</dd>
            <dt><code>baudelaire check</code></dt>
            <dd>Compile every page and report broken internal links without writing output. A fast CI gate.</dd>
            <dt><code>baudelaire new &lt;path></code></dt>
            <dd>Scaffold a content file with starter frontmatter, e.g. <code>baudelaire new content/posts/hello.typ</code>.</dd>
            <dt><code>baudelaire init [dir]</code></dt>
            <dd>Scaffold a whole project (config, content, a template, and a stylesheet) into <code>dir</code>, or the current directory.</dd>
            <dt><code>baudelaire clean</code></dt>
            <dd>Remove the output and cache directories.</dd>
          </dl>
          <h3>Global flags</h3>
          <dl>
            <dt><code>--config &lt;path></code></dt>
            <dd>Config file to read (default <code>config.kdl</code>).</dd>
            <dt><code>--root &lt;dir></code></dt>
            <dd>Change into <code>dir</code> first, so every relative path resolves under it.</dd>
            <dt><code>--profile &lt;name></code></dt>
            <dd>Apply a named profile from the <code>profiles</code> block.</dd>
            <dt><code>--out &lt;dir></code></dt>
            <dd>Override the output directory.</dd>
            <dt><code>--base-url &lt;url></code></dt>
            <dd>Override the site URL, useful for preview deploys.</dd>
            <dt><code>--drafts</code>, <code>--future</code></dt>
            <dd>Include draft or future-dated pages.</dd>
            <dt><code>--no-cache</code></dt>
            <dd>Ignore the cache and rebuild everything.</dd>
            <dt><code>--strict-links &lt;bool></code></dt>
            <dd>Treat broken internal links as errors (default) or warnings.</dd>
            <dt><code>-v / -vv</code>, <code>-q</code></dt>
            <dd>More or less output.</dd>
          </dl>
